# [SONNET-4.6] sq-zgbso.2 — ODRL stateless core: stratum B.
# Input: the serialized closure of stratum A (action facts + atomicSat + lcSat(or)).
#
# NAF in this stratum is over stratum A's COMPLETE atomicSat set (safe by stratification):
#   - odrlx:andSubUnsat — odrl:and LC has an unsatisfied sub-constraint
#   - odrlx:anyRuleConstrUnsat — a RULE (permission OR prohibition — any subject
#     carrying odrl:constraint) has an unsatisfied atomic constraint
#
# Also derives (positive, no NAF on derived facts):
#   - odrlx:prohibMatches — UNCONSTRAINED prohibition matches the request
#   - auth:deny* triples  — denial emit for matched unconstrained prohibitions
# (CONSTRAINED prohibitions match in stratum C, which needs this stratum's complete
#  anyRuleConstrUnsat; the grant rules live in stratum D so their NAF sees the
#  complete prohibMatches.)

@prefix odrl:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .
@prefix auth:  <https://sparq.dev/ns/auth#> .
@prefix odrlx: <https://sparq.dev/ns/odrlx#> .
@prefix log:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

# ── odrl:and logical constraint: unsatisfied sub-constraint witness ───────────
# NAF is over stratum A's atomicSat, which is complete before this stratum runs.
{ ?lc odrl:and ?c .
  ?req a odrl:Request .
  ?S log:notIncludes { ?c odrlx:atomicSat ?req } . }
=> { ?lc odrlx:andSubUnsat ?req } .

# ── rule (permission OR prohibition): any unsatisfied atomic constraint ───────
# Only atomic constraints are checked here (they carry odrl:leftOperand; LCs do not).
# ?rule binds ANY subject carrying odrl:constraint — permissions and prohibitions
# alike — so both stratum C (prohibition match) and stratum D (grants) NAF over it.
# NAF is over stratum A's atomicSat (complete before this stratum).
{ ?rule odrl:constraint ?c . ?c odrl:leftOperand ?lo .
  ?req a odrl:Request .
  ?S log:notIncludes { ?c odrlx:atomicSat ?req } . }
=> { ?rule odrlx:anyRuleConstrUnsat ?req } .

# ── prohibition match + deny emission (unconstrained prohibitions only) ───────
# An unconstrained prohibition (no odrl:constraint) is matched by checking only
# action / target / assignee against the request. NAF is over the INPUT predicate
# odrl:constraint, which is complete before any stratum (input-level negation).
{ ?pol odrl:prohibition ?proh .
  ?proh odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?act odrlx:denyMode ?denyMode .
  ?req a odrl:Request ; odrl:action ?act ; odrl:target ?tgt ; odrl:assignee ?party .
  ?S log:notIncludes { ?proh odrl:constraint ?anyc } . }
=> { ?proh odrlx:prohibMatches ?req . ?party ?denyMode ?tgt . } .
